    rdfs:label "Evidence for Gum Benzoin used in Perfumery, Pomades & Essential Oils: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 1064"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "STYRAX BENZOIN: The Benzoin Tree. The Resin = lubán (Ind. bazárs), hussí, shambiráni, kaminian, etc. A small tree of the Malay Archipelago, important as yielding the true Benzoin or Gum Benjamin of commerce. This substance appears to have been first mentioned by Ibn Batuta (Voy., etc., Fr. ed. 1858, iv., 228, 240), who visited Sumatra (A.D. 1325–49). He call..."@en ;
